est.cli.v2 JSON protocol envelope. When a command runner returns an envelope with an invalid or unexpected schema (e.g. \\\"forest.cli.v1\\\"), missing envelope fields (schema, command, args, exit), or trailing JSON data, Collect must reject the envelope with a *CLIError identifying the schema mismatch or envelope error, and terminate collection without accepting invalid data. Failing example: execute collector.Collect where the runner outputs an envelope with Schema: \\\"forest.cli.v1\\\" or with missing schema field or trailing JSON; today collector_test.go only tests command mismatch (TestCLICollectorRejectsEnvelopeCommandMismatch) and exit status failures; zero tests exercise schema mismatch or envelope JSON structural validation. Acceptance: a Builder adds test cases in collector_test.go asserting that Collect returns a *CLIError with the message mentioning invalid schema when the envelope schema is not \\\"forest.cli.v2\\\", and fails when envelope top-level fields are missing or trailing JSON is present. Observed: collector.go:297-300 and collector.go:356-361 check the schema and top-level envelope fields, but grep reveals no test references invalid schema or envelope field parsing errors. Required: unit tests in collector_test.go covering envelope schema mismatch, missing required envelope keys, and trailing JSON in command output. Proposed test-work: add collector tests in collector_test.go verifying that envelopes with incompatible schema versions, missing top-level keys, or trailing JSON are rejected with a CLIError.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:51:10.542Z\",\n      \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"text\": \"took\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:49:05.527Z\",\n  \"promotions\": [\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:49:05.527Z\",\n      \"by\": \"none\",\n      \"spec\": \"Defend the public Collector.Collect protocol boundary without changing forest.cli.v2 policy. Using the existing injectable CommandRunner, return malformed envelopes and assert a command-attributed CLIError rather than an accepted snapshot. Cover unsupported schema, non-object/malformed JSON, trailing JSON, omitted required envelope fields, and null args. Keep the existing command-mismatch and command-failure tests; do not duplicate them. Cases must use otherwise-valid command data so each fails for its intended reason. Prove collection stops at the offending command and valid envelopes still succeed. No source-string assertions, new decoding abstraction, or mock-echo tests. Run focused collector tests and repository checks.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:28.732Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:51:10.542Z\",\n  \"derived\": {\n    \"terminal\": false,\n    \"waiting\": false,\n    \"open\": true,\n    \"live\": true,\n    \"takeable\": false\n  }\n}\n"}],"details":{}}}
