erval wait plus up to a 30s collection bound). Correctness traced: classifyFreshness still marks explicit errors stale immediately and unknown when no success exists; pageView now uses freshnessWindow for both selected and fleet instances; ancestry holds (HEAD parent is origin/master 674894f). New freshness_test.go covers selected/fleet windows, interval changes, explicit-error staleness, unknown state, and no-overlap slow success; go test -race and go vet pass. No blocking findings.\",\"time\":\"2026-09-04T19:56:13Z\"}\n\n=== 7b7865905d8b6410fe17cf403e0ba269be08807d ===\n{\"schema\":\"forest.verdict.v1\",\"revision\":\"e15fcacd647bb54155c7056356bf34e2238497e6\",\"verdict\":\"approve\",\"summary\":\"Test-only refactor: extract scanDevelopmentRoot from scanDevelopmentRoots and replace the host-dependent TestDiscoverLocalInstances with a deterministic mocked-checkout test. Production discovery behavior is unchanged; go test and go vet pass; Revision fast-forwards origin/master.\",\"time\":\"2026-09-04T17:54:59Z\"}\n\n=== ba2f874b1f09253ac5515ba846452c56bdd55611 ===\n{\"schema\":\"forest.verdict.v1\",\"revision\":\"ca9e23795abebbe11ec519332a79b9c1d96d9ae2\",\"verdict\":\"approve\",\"summary\":\"Checks test and vet pass with exit 0. Revision ca9e2379 is a fast-forward of origin/master (d570c11). Diff changes discovery.go and discovery_test.go: scanDevelopmentRoot now recognizes forest.yaml-declared checkouts in addition to legacy .forest+executable forest checkouts, and resolves the Forest binary as repo-local, then PATH, then parent/iron-forest/forest. New tests cover forest.yaml discovery, non-executable local fallback to factory, and PATH preference. No blocking correctness, security, or maintainability findings.\",\"time\":\"2026-09-04T19:01:18Z\"}\n\n=== a03a3b8142e3f11144466d57666fcfb4bfac33e7 ===\n{\"schema\":\"forest.verdict.v1\",\"revision\":\"fbb9338e93e8b83963ed35a6fa287adb2fc8e5c6\",\"verdict\":\"approve\",\"summary\":\"Checks test and vet pass (exit 0). Revision fast-forwards origin/master e15fcacd. Diff preserves explicit inventory during discovery reconciliation (app.go App.discovered) and gives startup-discovered instances exactly one worker (instanceWorker.started); added tests cover single-worker startup, worker cleanup after prune, and explicit retention. go test -race also passes. No blocking findings.\",\"time\":\"2026-09-04T18:28:42Z\"}\n\n=== 02d66c9e20e9af66dd69131dc1e2557d12949063 ===\n{\"schema\":\"forest.verdict.v1\",\"revision\":\"0f61b4007878a9bd93ad014a750221fbcb5aff62\",\"verdict\":\"approve\",\"summary\":\"Checks test (go test ./...) and vet (go vet ./...) both pass with exit 0. The Revision gates the fleet and instance HTMX polling triggers with [document.hidden === false], so background polls are skipped while the tab is hidden and resume when visible; the vendored HTMX 2.0.9 parser/evaluator confirms the filter cancels poll issuance when the expression is not true and still reschedules the next tick. templates_test.go verifies both rendered triggers contain the visibility gate. Fast-forward from origin/master fbb9338 is verified; no blocking findings.\",\"time\":\"2026-09-04T18:45:43Z\"}\n\n=== d0c2f4812d3f0a66dcfa43888527ac9953752ffd ===\n{\"schema\": \"forest.verdict.v1\", \"revision\": \"c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a\", \"verdict\": \"approve\", \"summary\": \"Checks passed (go test ./... and go vet ./...). Test-only revision adds coverage for audit divergence stale override rendering: divergent pass/trusted render class stale with the result text, while equal or missing revision pairs retain the ok class. Verified against auditView in view.go and by running the new subtests; revision is one commit ahead of origin/master and fast-forwards cleanly.\", \"time\": \"2026-09-04T19:28:49Z\"}\n\n=== 4ce6f00dd55b995475e196c4b7657b8c21eee357 ===\n{\"schema\":\"forest.verdict.v1\",\"revision\":\"08955b8839d45c3181286c798280f9f2d3aa422e\",\"verdict\":\"changes\",\"summary\":\"Stale revision: 0