"forest/canopy-tester-envelope-schema-validation/envelope-validation\",\"revision\":\"08955b8839d45c3181286c798280f9f2d3aa422e\",\"time\":\"2026-09-04T19:53:05Z\",\"tracker\":\"powder\"}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788552378553},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_60ede2381862400b9edec8a9","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"08955b8839d45c3181286c798280f9f2d3aa422e\nIron Forest Builder <builder@forest.invalid>\ntest(canopy): prove CLI envelope schema and malformed rejection\n\n collector_test.go | 122 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--\n 1 file changed, 118 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)\n--- master ---\n73d14896ee481447a80453dbd97b57461e8383d6 fix(canopy): derive freshness window from collection cycle budget\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788552378553},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The request payload has `tracker: powder`. So I need to run Powder's doctor/show/take flow from the shared skill. Let me read the powder skill.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The request payload has `tracker: powder`. So I need to run Powder's doctor/show/take flow from the shared skill. Let me read the powder skill.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Evidence verified:\n- Verdict committer: `Iron Forest Verifier <verifier@forest.invalid>` ✓\n- Verdict: `\"verdict\":\"changes\"`, revision `08955b8839d45c3181286c798280f9f2d3aa422e` ✓\n- Request committer: `Iron Forest Builder <builder@forest.invalid>` ✓\n- Request payload: subject `canopy-tester-envelope-schema-validation`, branch `forest/canopy-tester-envelope-schema-validation/envelope-validation`, revision matches, `tracker: powder` ✓\n\nThe tracker is `powder`, so I must run Powder's doctor/show/take flow. Let me read the Powder skill.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8aa6869736004d0f889def65","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/phaedrus/development/misty-step/canopy/.forest/worktrees/1788552344330660153-fixer/agents/_shared/skills/powder/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731","usage":{"input":276,"output":271,"cacheRead":15872,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":36,"totalTokens":16419,"cost":{"input":0.000013800000000000002,"output":0.0000271,"cacheRead":0.00015872,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00019962000000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788552378553,"responseId":"gen-1788552378-TreQ6vlbze7Tv4SRxFqt","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8aa6869736004d0f889def65","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: powder\ndescription: >\n  Powder is the exclusive-work ledger. Use when listing takeable jobs\n  for this repository, taking a job, asking the operator, or completing\n  work with proof after an approve Gate.\n---\n\n# Powder\n\nPowder stores jobs. Take one. Finish it. Write proof.\n\n## Client contract\n\nOrigin resolves from `POWDER_URL`, then `~/.config/powder/config`; there is no\ndefault. Remote origins require HTTPS; HTTP is loopback-only. `POWDER_AGENT` is\noptional audit metadata. Managed workers pass the\nexact canonical label `forest-misty-step/powder`, but this label never\nauthorizes a lease or any other operation. `POWDER_API_KEY` is transport\nauthentication.\n\nRun `powder doctor [--agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\"]` before selection to verify the\nconfigured origin and service. If the check fails, do not call Powder. GitHub\nIssues remain the Tracker.\n\nEach successful `powder take` returns a flat JSON Job plus a per-job\n`claim_token` made from 32 random bytes encoded as base64url. Only its SHA-256\nhash is stored in `jobs.lease_token_hash`. A live job returns `held` unless\nthe CLI presents that job's matching stored claim, which resumes it. An audit\nlabel never grants resume. The claim token is capability for only that lease.\n\nThe CLI stores claim tokens privately under XDG state by validated origin and\njob id, resumes by job id, and sends them automatically. It never prints\nclaims, and list/show/logs/notes never expose them. `release`, `renew`, `ask`,\n`done`, live-job field edits, and live `abandon` require the claim; missing is\n`claim_required`, and mismatch or expiry is `invalid_claim`. `note` stays\nreport-authorized and claim-independent. Free-job patching or abandon uses\n`promote` authority without a claim. Tokens are deleted after release, ask,\ndone, or abandon.\n\n## Factory loop\n\n1. When `POWDER_AGENT` is set, run\n   `powder list --mine \"$POWDER_AGENT\" --repo <forest.yaml repo>`. Treat\n   `--mine` as an audit-label filter, never as resumable authority. A live\n   candidate is resumable only when `powder take <id> [--agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\"]`\n   succeeds with the private claim stored for this origin and job id, and no\n   `forest/<id>/*` branch exists. When `POWDER_AGENT` is unset, attempt\n   resumption only for a job id supplied by the managed run or current branch;\n   otherwise continue to takeable selection.\n2. `powder list --takeable --repo <forest.yaml repo>`\n3. `powder show <id>`\n   The spec is the work. Empty spec is not takeable. Show never contains a\n   claim token.\n4. `powder take <id> [--agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\"]`\n   Do this before creating a branch. A successful take stores the private\n   claim. A live job returns `held`, even under the same audit label; do not\n   interpret `held` as permission from the label. Keep a published Subject\n   held for the Kernel completion loop, and release only a failed or\n   unpublished Builder attempt.\n5. A Fixer uses the same Subject's private claim by job id before branch\n   mutation; the audit label is only metadata.\n6. Publish with schema v2, `tracker` set to the source actually selected\n   (`github` or `powder`), and branch `forest/<id>/<slug>`. Every Subject uses\n   that shape, including GitHub Issue numbers.\n7. Agents do not call `powder done`. The Kernel completes the current\n   Git-landed Subject only when request evidence has `tracker: powder`, using\n   the approved Revision as proof. The CLI clears the private claim after\n   completion or any release/ask/abandon.\n\nMultiple distinct jobs may be held under the same managed audit label. Every\nclaim authorizes only its own job; managed workers and the Kernel do not mint\nor share authority from the label.\n\n\n## Verbs\n\n```\npowder list --takeable --repo REPO\npowder list --mine AGENT --repo REPO\npowder show ID\npowder take ID\npowder release ID\npowder ask ID --question '...'\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788552380895},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The request payload says tracker: powder. I need to run `powder doctor [--agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\"]`, then `powder show <subject>` using subject `canopy-tester-envelope-schema-validation`, require job's repo to match forest.yaml (`misty-step/canopy`), non-terminal, then `powder take <subject>` before checking out or editing the branch.\n\nLet me check environment for POWDER_AGENT and run doctor.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The request payload says tracker: powder. I need to run `powder doctor [--agent \\\"$POWDER_AGENT\\\"]`, then `powder show <subject>` using subject `canopy-tester-envelope-schema-validation`, require job's repo to match forest.yaml (`misty-step/canopy`), non-terminal, then `powder take <subject>` before checking out or editing the branch.\\n\\nLet me check environment for POWDER_AGENT and run doctor.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Tracker is `powder`. I must run Powder's doctor/show/take flow. Let me check the environment and run doctor."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_a74431515e2c495aa0e018e8","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/phaedrus/development/misty-step/canopy/.forest/worktrees/1788552344330660153-fixer && echo \"POWDER_AGENT=${POWDER_AGENT:-<unset>}\" && echo \"POWDER_URL=${POWDER_URL:+<set>}\" && echo \"POWDER_API_KEY=${POWDER_API_KEY:+<set>}\" && command -v powder && powder --version 2>&1 | head -2"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731","usage":{"input":1278,"output":272,"cacheRead":16128,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":99,"totalTokens":17678,"cost":{"input":0.00006390000000000001,"output":0.000027200000000000004,"cacheRead":0.00016128,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00025238}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788552380896,"responseId":"gen-1788552380-MC8zdf7r1Vgz8l9S3CHH","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a74431515e2c495aa0e018e8","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"POWDER_AGENT=forest-misty-step/canopy\nPOWDER_URL=<set>\nPOWDER_API_KEY=<set>\n/home/phaedrus/.local/bin/powder\n{\n  \"code\": \"usage\",\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788552382984},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ea3df0e31c7844168ad26ddb","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/phaedrus/development/misty-step/canopy/.forest/worktrees/1788552344330660153-fixer && powder doctor --agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731","usage":{"input":75,"output":86,"cacheRead":17664,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":17825,"cost":{"input":0.0000037500000000000005,"output":0.0000086,"cacheRead":0.00017664000000000002,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00018899000000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788552382985,"responseId":"gen-1788552383-3emJJLYVXEd6pDCryFyr","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ea3df0e31c7844168ad26ddb","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"origin\": \"https://sanctum.tail5f5eb4.ts.net:10001\",\n  \"origin_source\": \"environment\",\n  \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n  \"agent_source\": \"flag\",\n  \"api_key\": \"present\",\n  \"health\": \"ok\",\n  \"ready\": \"ok\"\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1