 },\n  \"ask\": null,\n  \"proof\": null,\n  \"abandoned\": false,\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:32.824Z\",\n      \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788550542912867580-tester (git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a), running PID 704790 build unknown\\nSurface: collector.go:297 (cliCollector.runJSON), collector.go:343 (decodeCLIEnvelope), collector.go:138 (cliCollector.Collect). Behaviors: Canopy relies strictly on the forest.cli.v2 JSON protocol envelope. When a command runner returns an envelope with an invalid or unexpected schema (e.g. \\\"forest.cli.v1\\\"), missing envelope fields (schema, command, args, exit), or trailing JSON data, Collect must reject the envelope with a *CLIError identifying the schema mismatch or envelope error, and terminate collection without accepting invalid data. Failing example: execute collector.Collect where the runner outputs an envelope with Schema: \\\"forest.cli.v1\\\" or with missing schema field or trailing JSON; today collector_test.go only tests command mismatch (TestCLICollectorRejectsEnvelopeCommandMismatch) and exit status failures; zero tests exercise schema mismatch or envelope JSON structural validation. Acceptance: a Builder adds test cases in collector_test.go asserting that Collect returns a *CLIError with the message mentioning invalid schema when the envelope schema is not \\\"forest.cli.v2\\\", and fails when envelope top-level fields are missing or trailing JSON is present. Observed: collector.go:297-300 and collector.go:356-361 check the schema and top-level envelope fields, but grep reveals no test references invalid schema or envelope field parsing errors. Required: unit tests in collector_test.go covering envelope schema mismatch, missing required envelope keys, and trailing JSON in command output. Proposed test-work: add collector tests in collector_test.go verifying that en